    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay fine, no glue. but i'm really worried about the rust and getting tetanus or something since the shovel was old. if i can't get to a clinic until next week, is there any way i can just take some extra antibiotics i have left over from a previous prescription to make sure nothing grows in there? or maybe some high dose vitamin c to boost my immune system? i just need to be sure i'm safe until i can actually see someone.",
