      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Taking antibiotics over-the-counter without a prescription can be ineffective and even lead to antibiotic resistance. Vitamin C supplements are not a substitute for proper medical treatment. The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) and the American Academy of Family Physicians (AAFP) recommend that patients at risk for tetanus receive post-exposure prophylaxis (PEP) as soon as possible, which typically involves a tetanus shot from a healthcare provider.",
